{"amendments":[{"body":"Correctness: `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs:331-340` seeds missing `animal.reserve_g` from existing shrimp biomass during the v3->v4 migration. That changes the physical state of every migrated save instead of preserving it. `reserve_g` is documented as post-feeding retained reserve, not structural shrimp biomass (`crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:94-99`), and it is counted as separate N/C mass in the budget (`crates/tank_core/src/types/budget.rs:246-248`, `crates/tank_core/src/types/budget.rs:331-333`) and later spent for hatching/maturation (`crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:641-651`) or exported on shrimp removal (`crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:402-408`). A schema-3 save with existing shrimp therefore gains free reserve, extra total mass, and potentially immediate reproduction/maturation progress just by loading. The migration should preserve old behavior by leaving `reserve_g` at its serde default of `0.0`, or by introducing a separate non-budgeted compatibility/display field if an inspectable value is still desired.","rationale":"Old saves need to remain behaviorally equivalent after migration. The current migration invents new matter and changes downstream gameplay state solely because the save crossed a schema boundary."}],"summary":"Reviewed the changed save/shrimp implementation and tests. Found 1 correctness issue: the new v3->v4 migration manufactures shrimp reserve mass for legacy saves, which changes budgets and gameplay behavior on load."}